keywords:
  - nonlinear mixed-effects models
  - SAEM
  - ordinary differential equations
  - population models
  - Python
abstract: >
  PySAEM estimates nonlinear mixed-effects models of ordinary differential equations in Python
  with the stochastic approximation expectation-maximisation algorithm (SAEM). The model is
  written as Python functions or as equations, read into symbolic equations and compiled with
  Numba. A fit returns the estimates with their standard errors, the likelihood, information
  criteria and diagnostics.
